      "notes": "Linear optical switch; its slider shares the Orange's bump, cleared by a notch in the housing. Third generation of Bloody's Light Strike optical switches: the stem sits in a cuboid shroud for dust and spill resistance, every switch carries its own stabilizer bar, and a crystal prism spreads light from the LED on the PCB. The one-piece body is not meant to be opened."
